      "candidate_sources": {
        "README.md": "# Transfer retry panel with decoded progress\n\nThis workspace selects files, starts transfers, records queue and progress\nhistory, and paints progress for the open panel. Run it with Node v16.20.2; it\nhas no dependencies. `src/workspace.js` exports the workspace and the source\nhelpers used by the host application.\n\nSelecting a file creates a visit. Retry replaces the physical attempt without\nopening another visit. Selecting the same file again does open another visit.\nThe feed object is shared by attempts and visits for that file. Its `start()`\nmethod may synchronously emit cached data, and `decode(packet)` may return a\nvalue or a Promise.\n\n`recordProgress` appends transfer history. `showProgress` paints the panel.\nThe queue adapter in `src/queue.js` shows how those two outputs currently relate\nto a visit. Queue records, notices, cancellation, retry, navigation, and cleanup\nretain their existing behavior. Queue records remain\n`{fileId, attemptId, visitId, kind}` unless a separate authorization adds\n`byteCount` from `file.size`.\n\nOne startup window is relevant to this maintenance request: `start()` may emit\nmore than one packet synchronously. A `showProgress` callback may select or hide\nanother visit before `start()` returns, while its caller has not yet received\nthe returned cleanup handle.\n\nThe same feed API also has a diagnostic consumer in `src/telemetry.js`.\nIt is not the panel and must keep its existing behavior while the panel defect\nis repaired. `src/progress-source.js` is the host-visible feed implementation;\nthe navigation and transfer modules show how ownership is handed off when a\nlistener is released. Host callbacks are synchronous unless their code returns\na Promise.\n",
        "VISIBLE_CHECKS.md": "# Public development checks\n\nRun `/runtime/node /workspace/tests/visible.mjs /workspace` from the isolated Action workspace. These examples were authored from the original maintenance request, README, and public modules before consulting any scorer/reference implementation. They are not a full specification.\n\nThe original task requires warm initial progress, preservation of transfer/retry/navigation/cleanup/audit/queue behavior, out-of-order full-frame display freshness, streaming, telemetry and subsequent uses. README states that startup may emit multiple packets before returning; a paint callback can synchronously hide or replace its visit before the cleanup handle returns. It also states visit-vs-attempt identity and shared-feed reuse. Public source distinguishes retained audit from current-visit painting and defines synchronous detach callbacks.\n\nExamples cover cached bootstrap, live streaming and the original queue shape; telemetry delta-only policy; retained audit and suppressed painting after departure; display freshness when two decodes settle in reverse order; admission during multi-packet startup after inline hide/switch; pending work across same-feed reopening; retry record/visit behavior including cancellation reentry; detach reentry; independent workspaces. A decoder's completion order does not invent new frame content rules. Checks are regression examples of the public obligations, not hidden scoring details. Preserve the public tests and configuration.\n",
        "package.json": "{\n  \"name\": \"transfer-progress-composition-v4\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \"16.20.2\"\n  }\n}\n",
        "src/notice.js": "// A queued notice describes the accepted attempt in its originating visit.\nexport function publishQueued(state, visit, handle) {\n  state.showQueued({ fileId: visit.file.id, attemptId: handle.attemptId,\n    visitId: visit.id, status: \"queued\" });\n}\n",
        "src/panel.js": "import { enqueueTransfer } from \"./queue.js\";\nimport { publishQueued } from \"./notice.js\";\n\nexport function releaseVisit(visit) {\n  const handle = visit.handle;\n  visit.handle = null;\n  if (handle) handle.cancel();\n}\n\nexport function selectFile(state, file) {\n  if (state.disposed) return null;\n  const requestId = ++state.nextVisit;\n  const previous = state.current;\n  state.current = null;\n  if (previous) releaseVisit(previous);\n  if (state.disposed || state.nextVisit !== requestId) return null;\n  const visit = { id: requestId, file, handle: null };\n  state.current = visit;\n  const handle = enqueueTransfer(state, visit, \"select\");\n  if (state.current === visit) {\n    visit.handle = handle;\n    publishQueued(state, visit, handle);\n  } else {\n    handle.cancel();\n  }\n  return handle;\n}\n\nexport function hidePanel(state) {\n  state.nextVisit++;\n  const previous = state.current;\n  state.current = null;\n  if (previous) releaseVisit(previous);\n}\n\nexport function disposeWorkspace(state) {\n  if (state.disposed) return;\n  state.disposed = true;\n  hidePanel(state);\n  for (const handle of state.tasks.values()) handle.cancel();\n}\n",
        "src/progress-source.js": "class ProgressEvent extends Event {\n  constructor(packet) {\n    super(\"progress\");\n    this.detail = packet;\n  }\n}\n\n// Removal commits before notifying the host. The host callback is synchronous\n// and may call workspace.select(...) or workspace.hide(). Repeated removal is inert.\nexport function createProgressFeed({ initialPacket, decode = value => value, onDetach = () => {} }) {\n  const target = new EventTarget();\n  const listeners = new Set();\n  const add = target.addEventListener.bind(target);\n  const remove = target.removeEventListener.bind(target);\n  target.addEventListener = (type, listener, options) => {\n    add(type, listener, options);\n    if (type === \"progress\") listeners.add(listener);\n  };\n  target.removeEventListener = (type, listener, options) => {\n    remove(type, listener, options);\n    if (type === \"progress\" && listeners.delete(listener)) onDetach();\n  };\n  return {\n    target,\n    decode,\n    start() {\n      const packet = typeof initialPacket === \"function\" ? initialPacket() : initialPacket;\n      if (packet !== undefined) target.dispatchEvent(new ProgressEvent(packet));\n    },\n    emit(packet) { target.dispatchEvent(new ProgressEvent(packet)); },\n  };\n}\n",
        "src/progress.js": "// The source is shared by visits of the same file. Decoding may settle later.\nexport function watchTransferProgress(feed, receive, record, isCurrent = () => true) {\n  let stopped = false;\n  let nextPacket = 0;\n  let lastDisplayed = 0;\n  const active = () => !stopped && isCurrent();\n  const listener = event => {\n    // Startup can reenter navigation before our cleanup handle is returned.\n    if (!active()) return;\n    const packet = ++nextPacket;\n    const deliver = frame => {\n      // Admitted work retains its history even after its owner departs.\n      record(frame);\n      if (active() && packet > lastDisplayed) {\n        lastDisplayed = packet;\n        receive(frame);\n      }\n    };\n    const decoded = feed.decode(event.detail);\n    if (decoded && typeof decoded.then === \"function\") decoded.then(deliver);\n    else deliver(decoded);\n  };\n  feed.target.addEventListener(\"progress\", listener);\n  feed.start();\n  return () => {\n    if (stopped) return;\n    stopped = true;\n    feed.target.removeEventListener(\"progress\", listener);\n  };\n}\n",
        "src/queue.js": "import { createTransfer } from \"./transfer.js\";\n\n// Queue records are retained even when their originating panel visit ends.\nexport function makeQueueRecord(file, attemptId, visitId, kind) {\n  return { fileId: file.id, attemptId, visitId, kind };\n}\n\nexport function enqueueTransfer(state, visit, kind) {\n  const attemptId = ++state.nextAttempt;\n  state.record(makeQueueRecord(visit.file, attemptId, visit.id, kind));\n  const progress = {\n    isCurrent() { return state.current === visit; },\n    record(frame) { state.recordProgress({ fileId: visit.file.id, attemptId, frame }); },\n    receive(frame) {\n      if (state.current === visit) state.showProgress({ fileId: visit.file.id, attemptId, frame });\n    },\n  };\n  const handle = createTransfer(visit.file, attemptId, state.transport, state.onCancel, progress);\n  state.tasks.set(attemptId, handle);\n  return handle;\n}\n",
        "src/retry.js": "import { enqueueTransfer } from \"./queue.js\";\nimport { publishQueued } from \"./notice.js\";\n\n// A retry click accepts exactly one command for the current visit and file.\nexport function retryTransfer(state) {\n  const visit = state.current;\n  if (!visit || !visit.handle || state.disposed) return null;\n  const previous = visit.handle;\n  previous.cancel();\n  const handle = enqueueTransfer(state, visit, \"retry\");\n  if (state.current === visit) visit.handle = handle;\n  else handle.cancel();\n  if (state.current === visit) publishQueued(state, visit, handle);\n  return handle;\n}\n",
        "src/telemetry.js": "// Diagnostics count live deltas only. A cached bootstrap is panel state, not a delta.\nexport function collectProgressTelemetry(feed, recordDelta) {\n  const listener = event => {\n    const deliver = frame => recordDelta(frame);\n    const decoded = feed.decode(event.detail);\n    if (decoded && typeof decoded.then === \"function\") decoded.then(deliver);\n    else deliver(decoded);\n  };\n  feed.start();\n  feed.target.addEventListener(\"progress\", listener);\n  return () => feed.target.removeEventListener(\"progress\", listener);\n}\n",
        "src/transfer.js": "import { watchTransferProgress } from \"./progress.js\";\n\nexport function createTransfer(file, attemptId, transport, onCancel, progress = {}) {\n  const controller = new AbortController();\n  let stopProgress = () => {};\n  controller.signal.addEventListener(\"abort\", () => {\n    stopProgress();\n    onCancel({ file, attemptId, signal: controller.signal });\n  }, { once: true });\n  transport({ file, attemptId, signal: controller.signal });\n  if (file.progressFeed) {\n    stopProgress = watchTransferProgress(file.progressFeed, progress.receive, progress.record,\n      () => !controller.signal.aborted && (!progress.isCurrent || progress.isCurrent()));\n    if (controller.signal.aborted) stopProgress();\n  }\n  return { file, attemptId, signal: controller.signal,\n    cancel() { if (!controller.signal.aborted) controller.abort(); } };\n}\n",
        "src/workspace.js": "import { selectFile, hidePanel, disposeWorkspace } from \"./panel.js\";\nimport { retryTransfer } from \"./retry.js\";\n\nexport function createTransferWorkspace({ transport, onCancel, record, showQueued, recordProgress = () => {}, showProgress = () => {} }) {\n  const state = { transport, onCancel, record, showQueued, recordProgress, showProgress, current: null,\n    nextVisit: 0, nextAttempt: 0, tasks: new Map(), disposed: false };\n  return {\n    select(file) { return selectFile(state, file); },\n    retry() { return retryTransfer(state); },\n    hide() { hidePanel(state); },\n    dispose() { disposeWorkspace(state); },\n    snapshot() {\n      const visit = state.current;\n      return { visitId: visit ? visit.id : null, fileId: visit ? visit.file.id : null,\n        attemptId: visit && visit.handle ? visit.handle.attemptId : null,\n        disposed: state.disposed, attempts: state.nextAttempt };\n    },\n  };\n}\n\nexport { createTransfer } from \"./transfer.js\";\nexport { makeQueueRecord, enqueueTransfer } from \"./queue.js\";\nexport { publishQueued } from \"./notice.js\";\nexport { releaseVisit, selectFile, hidePanel, disposeWorkspace } from \"./panel.js\";\nexport { retryTransfer } from \"./retry.js\";\nexport { collectProgressTelemetry } from \"./telemetry.js\";\nexport { createProgressFeed } from \"./progress-source.js\";\n",
        "tests/visible.mjs": "import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nconst root = process.argv[2];\nconst api = await import(pathToFileURL(path.join(root, 'src/workspace.js')).href);\nconst results = [];\nconst tick = async () => { for (let i=0;i<8;i++) await Promise.resolve(); };\nconst value = row => row.frame.value;\nfunction setup(extra = {}) {\n  const log = { records: [], queued: [], audit: [], shown: [], cancelled: [] };\n  let workspace;\n  workspace = api.createTransferWorkspace({\n    transport() {},\n    onCancel(row) { log.cancelled.push(row.attemptId); extra.onCancel?.(row,workspace); },\n    record(row) { log.records.push(row); },\n    showQueued(row) { log.queued.push(row); },\n    recordProgress(row) { log.audit.push(row); },\n    showProgress(row) { log.shown.push(row); extra.showProgress?.(row,workspace); },\n  });\n  return { workspace, log };\n}\nfunction feedMany(values) {\n  const target = new EventTarget();\n  const emit = packet => { const e = new Event('progress'); e.detail = packet; target.dispatchEvent(e); };\n  return { target, decode: x => x, start() { for (const v of values) emit({value:v}); }, emit };\n}\nasync function check(name, action) {\n  try { const actual = await action(); results.push({check:name,passed:true,actual}); }\n  catch (error) { results.push({check:name,passed:false,actual:error.actual ?? null,expected:error.expected ?? null,error:String(error.message)}); }\n}\nawait check('public_warm_bootstrap', async () => {\n  const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup();const f=api.createProgressFeed({initialPacket:{value:5}});\n  w.select({id:'A',size:10,progressFeed:f});\n  assert.deepEqual(l.shown.map(value),[5]);assert.deepEqual(l.audit.map(value),[5]);w.dispose();return {shown:[5],audit:[5]};\n});\nawait check('public_streaming_and_queue_shape', async () => {\n  const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup();const f=api.createProgressFeed({});w.select({id:'A',size:10,progressFeed:f});f.emit({value:8});\n  assert.deepEqual(l.shown.map(value),[8]);assert.deepEqual(l.audit.map(value),[8]);\n  assert.deepEqual(l.records,[{fileId:'A',attemptId:1,visitId:1,kind:'select'}]);w.dispose();return {shown:[8],records:l.records};\n});\nawait check('public_diagnostic_delta_policy', async () => {\n  const f=api.createProgressFeed({initialPacket:{value:1}});const deltas=[];\n  const stop=api.collectProgressTelemetry(f,x=>deltas.push(x.value));f.emit({value:2});stop();f.emit({value:3});\n  assert.deepEqual(deltas,[2]);return deltas;\n});\nawait check('public_admitted_decode_after_hide', async () => {\n  const tickets=[];const f=api.createProgressFeed({decode:x=>new Promise(resolve=>tickets.push(()=>resolve(x)))});\n  const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup();w.select({id:'A',progressFeed:f});f.emit({value:4});w.hide();tickets[0]();await tick();\n  assert.deepEqual(l.audit.map(value),[4]);assert.deepEqual(l.shown,[]);w.dispose();return {audit:[4],shown:[]};\n});\nawait check('public_out_of_order_full_frames', async () => {\n  const tickets=[];const f=api.createProgressFeed({decode:x=>new Promise(resolve=>tickets.push(()=>resolve(x)))});\n  const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup();w.select({id:'A',progressFeed:f});f.emit({value:1});f.emit({value:2});tickets[1]();await tick();tickets[0]();await tick();\n  assert.deepEqual(l.shown.map(value),[2]);assert.deepEqual(l.audit.map(value),[2,1]);w.dispose();return {shown:[2],audit:[2,1]};\n});\nawait check('public_inline_hide_during_multi_packet_start', async () => {\n  const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup({showProgress(row,host){if(row.frame.value===1)host.hide();}});const f=feedMany([1,2]);w.select({id:'A',progressFeed:f});\n  assert.deepEqual(l.shown.map(value),[1]);assert.deepEqual(l.audit.map(value),[1]);f.emit({value:3});assert.deepEqual(l.audit.map(value),[1]);assert.equal(w.snapshot().fileId,null);w.dispose();return {shown:[1],audit:[1]};\n});\nawait check('public_inline_switch_keeps_new_owner', async () => {\n  const b={id:'B',progressFeed:api.createProgressFeed({initialPacket:{value:7}})};let switched=false;\n  const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup({showProgress(row,host){if(!switched&&row.fileId==='A'){switched=true;host.select(b);}}});const f=feedMany([1,2]);w.select({id:'A',progressFeed:f});b.progressFeed.emit({value:8});\n  assert.deepEqual(l.shown.map(row=>row.fileId+':'+value(row)),['A:1','B:7','B:8']);\n  assert.deepEqual(l.audit.map(row=>row.fileId+':'+value(row)),['A:1','B:7','B:8']);assert.equal(w.snapshot().fileId,'B');w.dispose();return {shown:['A:1','B:7','B:8']};\n});\nawait check('public_same_feed_reopen_pending_decode', async () => {\n  const tickets=[];const f=api.createProgressFeed({decode:x=>new Promise(resolve=>tickets.push(()=>resolve(x)))});const file={id:'A',progressFeed:f};\n  const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup();w.select(file);f.emit({value:1});w.hide();w.select(file);f.emit({value:2});tickets[0]();tickets[1]();await tick();\n  assert.deepEqual(l.shown.map(value),[2]);assert.deepEqual(l.audit.map(value),[1,2]);assert.equal(w.snapshot().attempts,2);w.dispose();return {shown:[2],audit:[1,2]};\n});\nawait check('public_retry_retains_visit_and_record', async () => {\n  const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup();w.select({id:'A',size:11});const before=w.snapshot();w.retry();\n  assert.deepEqual(l.records,[{fileId:'A',attemptId:1,visitId:1,kind:'select'},{fileId:'A',attemptId:2,visitId:1,kind:'retry'}]);assert.equal(w.snapshot().visitId,before.visitId);assert.equal(w.snapshot().attemptId,2);assert.deepEqual(l.cancelled,[1]);w.dispose();return {records:l.records};\n});\nawait check('public_retry_cancellation_reentry', async () => {\n  let changed=false;const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup({onCancel(row,host){if(!changed){changed=true;host.select({id:'B'});}}});w.select({id:'A'});w.retry();\n  assert.deepEqual(l.records,[{fileId:'A',attemptId:1,visitId:1,kind:'select'},{fileId:'B',attemptId:2,visitId:2,kind:'select'},{fileId:'A',attemptId:3,visitId:1,kind:'retry'}]);assert.equal(w.snapshot().fileId,'B');assert.equal(w.snapshot().attemptId,2);assert.deepEqual(l.queued.map(row=>row.fileId),['A','B']);w.dispose();return {records:l.records,current:'B'};\n});\nawait check('public_detach_reentry_keeps_new_visit', async () => {\n  let changed=false;const b={id:'B',progressFeed:api.createProgressFeed({})};const {workspace:w,log:l}=setup();const f=api.createProgressFeed({onDetach(){if(!changed){changed=true;w.select(b);}}});w.select({id:'A',progressFeed:f});w.hide();b.progressFeed.emit({value:9});\n  assert.equal(w.snapshot().fileId,'B');assert.deepEqual(l.shown.map(value),[9]);w.dispose();return {current:'B',shown:[9]};\n});\nawait check('public_independent_workspaces', async () => {\n  const first=setup(),second=setup();first.workspace.select({id:'A'});second.workspace.select({id:'B'});first.workspace.dispose();\n  assert.equal(second.workspace.snapshot().fileId,'B');assert.equal(second.workspace.snapshot().disposed,false);second.workspace.retry();assert.equal(second.workspace.snapshot().attemptId,2);second.workspace.dispose();return {independent:true};\n});\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({passed:results.every(x=>x.passed),observations:results,regressions:[],unknowns:[]}));\n"
